  "overview": "**NASA Web Design System** is a light-first design system anchored on `#ffffff` canvas surfaces with `#0b0b0c` primary ink (19.7:1 contrast) and `#ff9d1e` brand accent.\n\nDisplay headlines pair `Helvetica Neue` with `System Sans` body copy (70px display down to 16px body), unified by `0px` razor-sharp architectural corners and stepped `#ffffff` -> `#f1f1f1` surface layering.\n\nMaintained by **NASA**. Source: live stylesheet extraction (https://nasa.github.io/nasawds-site/). Inventory: **42** colors, **14** typography steps, and **24** documented components (all rights reserved license).\n\n### Layout & Spacing\n- **Grid & Control Spacing**: Derived from 24 component tokens with documented paddings: `2rem`, `0.1rem 0.7rem`, `1rem 2rem`, `0`, `7px 10px`.\n- **Hierarchy**: Group controls cleanly within `#f1f1f1` cards; separate sibling sections using `color-mix(in srgb, #0b0b0c 14%, transparent)` hairlines rather than oversized whitespace.\n\n### Elevation & Depth\n- **Surface & Stroke Elevation**: Relies on crisp tonal contrast (`#ffffff` -> `#f1f1f1`) and `1px solid color-mix(in srgb, #0b0b0c 14%, transparent)` hairlines instead of heavy drop shadows.\n- **Interactive Lift**: Reserve higher surface brightness or focus outlines anchored on `#ff9d1e` for keyboard focus and active selection states.",
  "dos": "### Do\n- Anchor base views on `#ffffff` (light) with `#0b0b0c` primary text and `#0b0b0c` secondary labels.\n- Use `#ff9d1e` with `#0b0b0c` text (9.5:1) for primary CTAs, active tabs, and focus outlines.\n- Pair `Helvetica Neue` headings with `System Sans` body copy using documented weights and scale steps.\n- Enforce `0px` border-radius consistently across cards, inputs, and primary buttons.\n- Separate containers via `#f1f1f1` surface shifts and `color-mix(in srgb, #0b0b0c 14%, transparent)` hairlines cleanly.\n\n### Don't\n- Do not invert the base canvas out of light polarity without explicitly switching component text tokens.\n- Do not place low-contrast muted ink or raw white text on light accents without verifying >= 4.5:1 WCAG AA contrast.\n- Do not invent arbitrary brand colors, unverified fonts, or synthetic heavy shadows outside the palette above.\n- Do not apply rounded corners (> 0px) to structural containers or CTA buttons.\n- Do not truncate or drop border contrast on `input-error-message` fields and secondary buttons."
